 {
  "id": "hubtab",
  "type": "tab",
  "label": "Hub Core",
  "disabled": false,
  "info": "Every device is a pair of nodes: `device in` (what it publishes) and `device out` (what you send it).\n\n  direct mapping : device in  ->  device out                     (optionally through range / function nodes)\n  learned mapping: device in  ->  ml mapper  ->  device out      (record examples, train, predict)\n  manual control : inject     ->  device out\n\nContract: devices send /<device>/<param> <float 0..1> to UDP 9000 at ~20 Hz; the hub sends /<device>/set/<param>\nto the device's IP on UDP 9001. Devices are discovered from their traffic; nothing is configured by hand."
 },
