 {
  "id": "knottab",
  "type": "tab",
  "label": "Knot",
  "disabled": false,
  "info": "Retrieval instead of regression (CinemaKnot): record states of the devices as labelled entries, then let the live inputs recall the nearest one.\n\nRecipe with the dummy devices: Dummy Devices 'freeze m = 0.1', here 'cassette m = 0.9', 'record dark'. Then 0.5 / 0.5 / 'record mid', then 0.9 / 0.1 / 'record bright'. 'query on', then Dummy Devices 'resume sine': the cassette steps between the three recorded states instead of following a curve. Try 'randomness 0.5', and watch the onsets (a freeze button is a jump) re-ask the knot."
 },
 {
  "id": "dummytab",
  "type": "tab",
  "label": "Dummy Devices",
  "disabled": false,
  "info": "Two simulated devices talking to the hub over real UDP on this machine, so the hub path is exercised exactly as with hardware.\n  dummy TV       : publishes /tv/m at 20 Hz, slow sine + noise. Inject buttons freeze it at a value.\n  dummy cassette : listens on :9001 for /cassette/set/m, remembers it, echoes /cassette/m at 20 Hz.\nDelete this tab when real devices exist (a real cassette on this machine would also need port 9001)."
 },
